// D16778: a maker with an un-annotated parameter returns a hole lambda, and its calls deliver the
// result at two function types whose results differ. Each call builds a fresh closure, so the
// design owes both deliveries (D16753 is the parameterless maker).
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function adder(n) { return (a) => a + n }
// @@VALUE@@
adder(2)
// @@TYPE@@
(a: i32) => i32
// @@PROOF@@
print(v(3))
// @@WANT@@
5
// @@VALUE2@@
adder(2)
// @@TYPE2@@
(a: i32) => f64
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v(3) / 8.0)
// @@WANT2@@
0.625
